 existing tests continue to pass (OrderControllerTest original 4 tests, ShipmentControllerTest original 5 tests, CustomerControllerTest 3 tests)\n3. **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels CREATED shipments** ✓ - Tests cover cancelling active order (returns CANCELLED status) and cancelling CREATED shipments\n4. **Error responses are consistent with rest of API** ✓ - Uses ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException, returned through GlobalExceptionHandler with ApiError envelope\n5. **Repeated cancel succeeds, cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing, unknown order refused, shipment for cancelled order refused** ✓ - All covered by new tests:\n   - Repeated cancel: \"cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing\"\n   - Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment: \"returns 409 when cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment and changes nothing\"\n   - Unknown order: \"returns 404 when cancelling a non-existent order\"\n   - Shipment for cancelled order: \"returns 409 when creating a shipment for a cancelled order\"\n6. **No new Maven dependency** ✓ - Only used existing Spring and JUnit dependencies\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** ✓ - Only modified Order, OrderController, ShipmentController, ShipmentRepository, and ApiError files\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status` field to Order with default ACTIVE. This had to change to track order state.\n\n2. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added `findByOrderId()` method to query shipments by order ID. This was necessary to implement the cancel logic.\n\n3. **ApiError.kt** - Added two new ErrorCode entries: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for creating shipment on cancelled order) and `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` (for cancelling order with confirmed shipment). This was necessary to differentiate the two conflict scenarios.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - Added ShipmentRepository injection, added `cancel()` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order (404 if not found)\n   - Checks all shipments (409 if any CONFIRMED)\n   - Sets order to CANCELLED and cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Returns the order (200 OK)\n   - Idempotent: already-CANCELLED orders return immediately\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added OrderRepository injection, added check in create endpoint that rejects shipment creation if order exists and is CANCELLED (409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code). This was necessary to enforce the business rule.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 5 new test methods covering all cancel scenarios plus necessary setup for shipmentRepository injection and cleanup.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 1 new test method for creating shipment on cancelled order, plus necessary setup for orderRepository injection and cleanup.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met and all test cases are covered.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that cancels active orders with idempotent semantics, atomic all-or-nothing behavior when shipments are confirmed, and prevents shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — added OrderStatus enum and status field with ACTIVE default\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId() method to find shipments by order\n              ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED error codes\n              OrderController.kt — added cancel endpoint with shipment repository injection\n              ShipmentController.kt — added order repository injection and cancelled order check\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 5 tests for cancel scenarios\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 1 test for creating shipment on cancelled order\n\nTests         1. Cancel active order returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n              2. Cancelling active order cancels all CREATED shipments\n              3. Cancelling already-CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n              4. Cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n              5. Cancelling non-existent order returns 404\n              6. Creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\nVerification  ./mvnw test in sample-service/ directory: BUILD SUCCESS, 19 tests, 0 failures\n\nNot done      None\n```","ttft_ms":4003,"type":"result","duration_ms":133306,"uuid":"a48c4d03-d12e-420d-b7f1-5e9ffd374475","ttft_stream_ms":857,"time_to_request_ms":32,"first_content_frame_ms":1122,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

